From ca6fd176bfaf5868c8e3efe26f6f97686a50e95b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 17:21:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] Resolution: leave the 3D mode alone when the display
 mode is the viewer's

Choosing the arrangement for the display assumed the display mode would follow. It
does not follow when refresh rate adjusting is off: the mode is then whatever was
picked by hand in videoscreen.resolution, and nothing re-chooses it. Remapping the
arrangement there is worse than not remapping it - a hand-picked side-by-side mode
kept receiving a top-and-bottom frame, because the arrangement moved to suit a
frame-packing mode that was never going to be switched to. Kodi not being allowed
to change the mode has to mean not overriding how the frame is split either. Which
is also what makes a half mode testable: turn refresh rate adjusting off, pick the
sbs or tab mode in videoscreen.resolution, and both stay put.

ApplyStereoMode() ignored the same setting when nothing was playing, choosing a
resolution outright rather than through the search the player runs, and so
overwrote a hand-picked mode the moment 3D was toggled - before playback, which is
exactly when a viewer sets one up. Gate it the same way.

Neither of those helps while refresh rate adjusting is on, and there the half modes
cannot be reached at all: frame packing wins on size wherever it exists, which on
these EDIDs is every timing that has a half mode. So add
stereoscopicpreferframepacking to advancedsettings.xml, turning that preference
around, for exercising the half-resolution paths without giving up mode switching.
It applies to both the choice within a layout and the choice between the two
arrangements, or asking for the half modes would still land on frame packing
whenever the other arrangement only offers that.

The mode comparison behind those choices becomes one predicate rather than two
copies of the rule, since it now has a second reading of "better" to express.

Also correct where a 3D mode is selected by hand: the modes list dropped from the
whitelist in the previous commit feeds videoscreen.resolution, whose labels carry
the layout. videoscreen.screenmode only lists the rates within the resolution and
layout already chosen.

(cherry picked from commit e158ddee97fab3a31c6d7eebcf63945a5ad88eed)
